package shapes

Shapes for a small 2D game: balls, players and the methods that move
them.

A second paragraph, which only the overview shows.

CONSTANTS

MAX_BALLS = 64
    How many balls fit on the screen.

DEBUG_SHAPES = false

TYPES

Vec2 = [2]F32
    A 2D vector.

Pixels = distinct F32
    Screen pixels, kept apart from other numbers.

enum Dir : U8
    A compass direction.

    north
        Up the screen.
    south
    east = 4
        Values can skip ahead.
    west

    def opposite -> Dir
        The opposite direction.

union Shape = Ball | geo.Rect
    Something to draw.

struct Entity
    Shared by everything that moves.

    hp: Int = 100
        Hit points; 0 is dead.
    pos: Vec2

    def move(delta: Vec2)
        Moves by `delta`.

struct Player
    The one the player controls.

    using base: Entity
    name: String
        The name shown above the player.

    def heal(amount: Int)
        Restores `amount` hit points, up to 100.
    def self.create(name: String) -> Player
        A player at the origin.
    def kills -> Int

struct Ball
    A bouncing ball.

    pos: Vec2
    vel: Vec2 = [120.0, 80.0]
        Pixels per second.
    radius: F32 = 8.0

struct Pool($T, $N: Int)
    A fixed-size pool of `N` items.

    items: [N]T
    count: Int

    def push(x: T) -> Bool
        Adds `x`, unless the pool is full.

MODULES

module Greeter
    Gives a type a greeting.

    def greet -> String
        Says hello.

METHODS

def max_of(a: $T, b: T) -> T
    The larger of two values.

def clamp_int(x: Int) -> Int
    Clamps an `Int` to 0..10.

def clamp_f32(x: F32) -> F32
    Clamps an `F32` to 0..10.

overload :clamp, :clamp_int, :clamp_f32
    Clamps either kind of number.

def dump_shapes
    Does nothing outside debug builds.

MACROS

macro def counter(name: Symbol) -> Code
    Declares a method `name` that counts nothing yet.

EXTENSIONS

extend Shape
    def label -> String
        What the shape is called in messages.

extend Player
    def boost
        Doubles the player's speed.

extend String
    def loudness -> Int
        The size, shouted.
